From 082c83401663848fe8285b51da39aa78b413b841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen38-4090 <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:44:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/49] INT8 G64 V plane for the K8V4 cache (NINFER_KV_VI8,
 research24)

NINFER_KV_VI8=1 keeps K8V4's FP8-row K and Hadamard-rotated V but stores each rotated V row as INT8 G64 (256 code
bytes + four FP16 scales) instead of NVFP4 G16. Append, prompt, tiled and wide small-T verify, and the accepted-path
compaction take a VInt8 template flag chosen at launch; INT8 widens to FP16 exactly with the 0x6400 magic before the
scale multiply; the wide verify kernel keeps 3 packed stages so its arena stays under 99 KB. Knob off is unchanged
(e2e5 Spec-Bench-480 ids 482/482 identical to research23, fidelity identical). Engine fidelity of e2e5 with the knob:
prose 0.02646, code 0.10164, overall 0.06179, top-1 0.9256 (NVFP4 V: 0.02767 / 0.10341 / 0.06326, 0.9242).
